WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.288 --> 00:00:01.544
- I think I was like three,

00:00:01.544 --> 00:00:05.188
and I remember seeing the
head of a pig in a trash can

00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:07.588
and that's how you know you're Cuban.

00:00:07.588 --> 00:00:10.877
(upbeat cheerful music)

00:00:11.999 --> 00:00:13.391
- The 24th is the big day.

00:00:13.391 --> 00:00:15.667
- Traditionally, we celebrate Noche Buena.

00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.563
- And then the food is like the main dish.

00:00:17.563 --> 00:00:17.935
- Yeah.

00:00:17.935 --> 00:00:19.214
- Or the main attraction really.

00:00:19.214 --> 00:00:20.863
- When it comes to Christmastime,

00:00:20.863 --> 00:00:23.021
that's kind of when we
bust out the tamales.

00:00:24.861 --> 00:00:26.162
- What we do for our holidays is that

00:00:26.162 --> 00:00:28.902
sometimes we do have either
a turkey or we have chickens

00:00:28.902 --> 00:00:30.599
or we have tamales, but

00:00:30.599 --> 00:00:32.550
what Salvis are kind of famous for now

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:34.498
is panes con pavo or panes con gallina.

00:00:34.498 --> 00:00:36.542
- I'm from Venezuela,
I was born in Caracas.

00:00:36.542 --> 00:00:38.701
The piece de resistance

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:42.814
is usually the pan de
jamon and the hallacas,

00:00:42.814 --> 00:00:46.482
but the pan de jamon is like
super, super popular because

00:00:46.482 --> 00:00:48.777
you pretty much eat it with everything.

00:00:48.777 --> 00:00:50.429
- The amount of time that it takes

00:00:50.429 --> 00:00:53.054
to make these tamales is like a lot,

00:00:53.054 --> 00:00:56.045
so you do it like a week,
maybe two weeks in advance

00:00:56.045 --> 00:00:58.901
and you make like 500 tamales

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:00.829
and that takes a lot of work.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:04.471
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:04.708 --> 00:01:07.216
- So I present to you pierna de puerco,

00:01:07.216 --> 00:01:09.189
seasoned with onions and garlic.

00:01:09.189 --> 00:01:11.629
So aside from the pork
we would have like always

00:01:11.629 --> 00:01:15.437
arroz con frijoles,
platanitos fritos, tostones,

00:01:15.437 --> 00:01:17.732
the infamous caja china.

00:01:17.732 --> 00:01:20.606
Why it's called that I have no idea.

00:01:20.637 --> 00:01:23.420
- So this is a typical dish

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.463
that is served in
Colombia during Christmas.

00:01:25.463 --> 00:01:26.580
It's actually two things.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:29.063
It's bunuelos and the
other things is natilla.

00:01:29.063 --> 00:01:30.388
I think it originated in Spain

00:01:30.388 --> 00:01:31.851
but it's super popular in Colombia.

00:01:31.851 --> 00:01:35.215
- I brought, we call
it salpicao de frango.

00:01:35.215 --> 00:01:38.211
So it's basically chicken salad,

00:01:38.211 --> 00:01:40.487
and yeah in Brazil and in Colombia,

00:01:40.487 --> 00:01:43.971
and in South America it's
summer during the holidays,

00:01:43.971 --> 00:01:45.711
it's actually pretty hot.

00:01:46.776 --> 00:01:49.308
- Looks delicious, my mouth
just watered looking at it.

00:01:50.498 --> 00:01:51.487
- Salud!

00:01:51.487 --> 00:01:52.482
(speaking foreign language)

00:01:52.482 --> 00:01:53.414
- That's how you say.

00:01:53.414 --> 00:01:54.550
Hmm, this is perfect.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:55.318
- That is so good!

00:01:55.318 --> 00:01:56.222
We can't go wrong with this.

00:01:56.222 --> 00:01:59.498
- It looks like heavy but
it's not, it's super light.

00:01:59.498 --> 00:02:00.842
And it's cold.

00:02:00.842 --> 00:02:02.954
- Pork fest right here, latinos like meat.

00:02:02.954 --> 00:02:03.814
- It's delicious.

00:02:03.814 --> 00:02:06.022
I really like this, this
packs a punch of flavor.

00:02:06.022 --> 00:02:07.853
- Down in Miami, near the Caribbean,

00:02:07.853 --> 00:02:09.133
we eat a lot of bananas.

00:02:09.133 --> 00:02:11.173
We don't do much of the
corn thing so this is nice.

00:02:11.173 --> 00:02:13.430
- Oh my god yeah, that
sauce is gonna be the bomb.

00:02:13.430 --> 00:02:15.469
It's like meaty, like sauce from meat.

00:02:15.469 --> 00:02:16.769
- I'm not a really big fan of olives,

00:02:16.769 --> 00:02:18.953
but this is maybe the first time

00:02:18.953 --> 00:02:21.205
I've ever actually enjoyed
olive in something.

00:02:21.205 --> 00:02:22.553
- Are there radishes in here?

00:02:22.553 --> 00:02:24.859
- Yeah, we add radishes and
cucumbers for the crunch.

00:02:24.859 --> 00:02:25.769
- I love Christmas.

00:02:25.769 --> 00:02:26.585
- I love Christmas.

00:02:26.585 --> 00:02:28.716
- It's like the best,
you get the best food.

00:02:29.186 --> 00:02:31.065
- Everybody in the world
has beautiful dishes

00:02:31.065 --> 00:02:31.901
that they should share.

00:02:31.901 --> 00:02:33.781
- Latinos, there's so many of us.

00:02:33.781 --> 00:02:34.941
There's so many countries.

00:02:34.941 --> 00:02:38.517
And we don't really get to
taste each other's food often.

00:02:38.517 --> 00:02:39.957
- It's so funny 'cause like our countries

00:02:39.957 --> 00:02:40.909
are bordering each other.

00:02:40.909 --> 00:02:43.765
- I think the most precious,
valuable thing about this

00:02:43.765 --> 00:02:45.045
is the tradition.

00:02:45.045 --> 00:02:47.504
- Food is the way to
communicate with each other.

00:02:47.504 --> 00:02:48.968
That's the way humans do.

00:02:50.038 --> 00:02:51.886
So by eating each other's food,

00:02:51.886 --> 00:02:54.462
you can probably get a
little bit of their culture

00:02:54.462 --> 00:02:56.713
or a little bit more
understanding of their culture.

00:02:56.713 --> 00:02:57.249
- Yeah.

00:02:57.249 --> 00:02:58.515
- And that's an awesome thing.

00:02:58.515 --> 00:03:02.922
(upbeat salsa music)

